117.
TY  - JOUR
TI  - Results of floral surveys of industrial areas in West Berlin
AU  - Rebele, F.
T2  - Landschaft und Stadt
AB  - A total of 596 species of vascular plants has been recorded: 47.5% are native, 52.5% introduced species. The share of archeophytes (17%) and ephemerophytes (12.2%) is very high in the industrial areas, whereas the share of neophytic plants (23%) is about average for the inner urban area of Berlin. Species-are relationship of the flora of industrial areas shows high species diversity, especially of industrial derelict land. 99 species of the flora of the industrial areas (16.6%) are endangered or rare plants in West Berlin. Many species with high frequency are ruderal plant species of all successional stages. -from English summary DA
