AB  - Bird communities were studied in Hamburg in: areas of blocks of flats, a garden city zone, parks, woodland, and farmland. Distinct community structures were identified. The use of birds as indicators of habitat type is criticized. Using species diversity indices as a classification parameter presents problems: values grow with increasing number of species, especially in farmland areas, and diversity says nothing about the rarity of a bird community.-P.J.Jarvis DA
