AB  - On selected sites in the city of Mainz (Rhineland-Palatinum) the mapping of ants resulted in identifying 49 species. Within the developed areas they can be assigned to three different zones: relicts of natural lanscape such as calcareous shifting sands and floodplains (41 species) farmland (31 species) and urban sites (31 species). The study shows that species number decreases significantly along a gradient for habitats characteristic of the urban landscape. Responsible factors are not only limited to surface sealing and microclimatic factors but also include the impoverishment of structural elements within the urban biotopes. DA
