TI  - Harbours and industrial areas as hotspots of plant biodiversity in urban-industrial eco-systems - Botanical inventory of the harbour area of the river Rhine in Birsfelden, Switzerland
AU  - Lenzin, H.
AU  - Meier-Küpfer, H.
AU  - Schwegler, S.
AU  - Baur, B.
T2  - Naturschutz und Landschaftsplanung
AB  - In the harbour of the river Rhine in Birsfelden (comprising 54 ha) a variety of hardly used or abandoned areas are situated between economically used sites. In the hardly maintained habitats 230 plant species have been recorded with 64 species (28%) being regionally or nationally threatened and only 36 (15.6%) neophytes. On the basis of these findings habitat-specific particularities and their conservation problems are discussed. The results underline the great importance of extensively and diversely used harbours and industrial areas within the speciesrich urban-industrial ecosystems. These areas can be considered as important biodiversity hotspots with high conservation value. DA
