258.
TY  - JOUR
TI  - The fauna on vegetated roofs in Hamburg: a company of different habitat structures
AU  - Mecke, R.
AU  - Grimm, R.
T2  - Naturschutz und Landschaftsplanung
AB  - From May to August 1995 the fauna of seven vegetated flat roofs and one gravel-roof without vegetation was investigated and compared. Additionally, abiotic factors were measured and the vegetation was mapped. The animals identified belong to 18 orders and 97 families. Predominant were the orders of Acarina and Collembola, followed by Araneida, Rhynchota, Coleoptera, Hymenoptera and Diptera. Identified species comprise Saltatoria (3 species), Coleoptera (56), Aculeata (22), Syrphidae (12) and Noctuidae (4). The site conditions on some of the roofs differ considerably, varying from very dry to moist. Areas with high diversity of vegetation contained more species than roofs covered with uniform vegetation. Roofs with similar vegetation and site conditions contained a comparable fauna. Even on vegetated roofs in the very centre of Hamburg with significant distances from green areas, a high numbers of species, including some rare species, were found. Compared to traffic islands, however, the fauna of the roofs was considerably poorer. It can be concluded that roofs covered with vegetation ecologically enrich builtup areas, but they cannot completely compensate for the loss of open space. DA
