322.
TY  - JOUR
TI  - Seeking answers from above
AU  - Cooper, A.
T2  - Environment Business
AB  - In Germany, the inclusion of green roofs within new flat-roofed buildings is a legal requirement. Green roofs generally filter pollution, slow rainwater run-off, increase biodiversity and reduce energy needs and lowers carbon dioxide emissions. The Green Roof Forum helps to raise awareness of the technology through events while the Care4Air campaign encourages individuals and organizations to improve local air quality. The forum was able to establish the Green Roof Centre which is a research and demonstration hub to provide training and advice to construction professionals to give them more confidence in the technology. The center aims to encourage the involvement of local SMEs within the green-roof supply chain while successfully involving the Green Estate which is a local social enterprise specializing in turning neglected open space into aesthetic parkland space. Green Estate has then made this green technology more accessible to the domestic market. DA
