TI  - Occurrence and settlement of carabid beetles on an urban railway embankment - a contribution to urban ecology
AU  - Wahlbrink, D.
AU  - Zucchi, H.
T2  - Zoologische Jahrbucher: Abteilung fur Systematik, Okologie und Geographie der Tiere
AB  - In Osnabruck (Lower Saxony) the carabid fauna of an urban railway embankment was investigated. In total 52 species were captured. From the surrounding area to the city centre Shannon diversity and evenness decrease, the Berger-Parker-index increases. From the surrounding area to the city centre xerophilous carabids increase, hygrophilous and silvicolous carabids decrease. Body size of carabids on average decreases from the surroundings towards the city centre. Carabids were mostly macropterous. The brachypterous individuals of the city centre nearly exclusively belong to dimorphic/polymorphic species. Brachypterous species occur mainly in the surrounding area. -from Authors DA
