330.
TY  - JOUR
TI  - The colonization of a railway embankment leading into the city centre by short-winged beetles - Coleoptera, Staphylinidae
AU  - Wahlbrink, D.
AU  - Zucchi, H.
T2  - Zeitschrift fur Okologie und Naturschutz
AB  - In 1991 the staphylinid fauna of an urban railway embankment in Osnabruck (Germany, Lower Saxony) was investigated by means of 36 pitfall traps. Six sites representing a transect from the surrounding area to the city centre were sampled. In total 6483 individuals of 126 species were caught. Typical staphylinids of this urban railway embankment are eurytopic, ubiquitous or depend on special micro-habitats, eg nests of ants. From the periphery to the city centre, there is a decrease of species number, number of individuals, Margalef Index as well as Berger-Parker Index. For the most part the staphylinids captured on the railway embankment were of minor body size and of great dispersal power. The importance of urban rainway embankments as habitat or recruiting area is discussed. -from English summary DA
