TI  - Protection measures and management planning for the conservation of stagnant water bodies in the urban area of Bayreuth
AU  - Schlumprecht, H.
AU  - Stubert, I.
T2  - Landschaft und Stadt
AB  - Increasing pond area showed no significant positive influence on the numbers of all or endangered dragonfly species. Number of all odonate species and endangered species increased significantly with an increase of structural richness and decrease of exploitation. Most stagnant water bodies were spoilt by fish-farming, eutrophication and cultivation measures. One third had <4 odonate species, and only 7% had the typical and complete odonate community composition of Upper Frankonian water bodies. The proposed conservation program was divided into stagnant water body preservation, optimization planning, decrease of human exploitation and public relations work. Protection by nature conservation law was recommended for 10 ponds. The most important recommendations were the restructuring of shallow water zones, an increase in land-water-interface and a decrease of hobby fish-farming. -from English summary DA
