AB  - The fish fauna of the River Oker and three ponds in the Burgerpark near the city center of Braunschweig was sampled twice by means of electrofishing in September 1992 and March 1993. A total of 17 species out of 5 families were found. The fauna was dominated by euryoecious species. Roach Rutilus rutilus, perch Perca fluviatilis and bream Abramis brama represent more than 90% of the samples taken in the Oker, while roach Rutilus rutilus, rudd Scardinius erythrophthalmus and perch Perca fluviatilis represent more than 90% of the samples taken in the ponds. P. fluviatilis abundance decreased in the investigated ponds with increasing eutrophication level while the abundance, mean size and mean weight of roach R. rutilus increased. -from English summary DA
