TI  - Recultivation of the 'Landeskulturgraben' in Dessau as an example of the treatment of anthropogenic water bodies
AU  - Luderitz, V.V.
AU  - Hentschel, P.
T2  - Naturschutz und Landschaftsplanung
AB  - The 'Landeskulturgraben' is a small canal in the Biosphere Reserve 'Mittlere Elbe', the ecological functionality of which had been severly disturbed. In 1994 the canal bed structures were ecologically enhanced by different measures. By creating meanders, stillwater coves, course widenings, separated ponds and flattened banks the eco-morphological grade increased from 4.5 to 2.5. Water quality improved from class II - III (critically loaded) in 1994 to class II (moderately loaded) in 1995/1996. The number of macroinvertebrate species increased from 38 to 85, the number of water and amphibic plant species grew by 27. DA
