AB  - Study of Schlitz, Vogelsberg district, detected 841 species and subspecies, many of which are dependent on specific types of land use. Epilobium lanceolatum is found in a basalt quarry; while Digitaria ischaemon, Digitaria sanguinalis, Eragrostis minor and Berteroa incana are confined to the disused railway station site. Linaria repens flourishes on crushed limestone forest paths. Substantial changes in land utilization cover the last 100 or so years have affected more the range than the number of taxa. -R.Hardbottle DA
