644.
TY  - JOUR
TI  - The vegetation of long standing fallows and its change during a five year period
AU  - Hilbig, W.
T2  - Journal of Applied Botany
AB  - The vegetation development on abandoned fields, which were taken out from agricultural production for five years, was investigated during this five year period. The investigations were made on plots of two experimental farms and on normal fields in Bavaria. We considered uncropped fallows as well as fallows with unharvested clover-grass crop, both in mulched and unmulched variants. In the course of few years big changes in lifeform spectra could be observed. The dominant therophyts in the beginning of set aside were soon replaced by geophyts and above all by hemicryptophyts. In contrast to the low species number of wild plants in the crop fallow we find high species numbers in the uncropped fallow. But weeds with weak competition were soon replaced by dominant biennial and perennial ruderal and grassland species. Long term fallow cannot much contribute to the preservation of endangered weed species. DA
