AB  - This paper presents the results of lichenological studies done in central and northern parts of the Mrągów Lakeland. The analysed biota consists of 152 taxa, including 139 lichens and 13 non-lichenized, lichenicolous or saprobic fungi. Fourteen of the noted taxa are protected by law and 48 are on the list of endangered lichens in Poland. The biota includes such valuable species as Arthonia vinosa, Chaenotheca chlorella, Chrysothrix candelaris, Diplotomma alboatrum, Fellhanera gyrophorica, Lecania erysibe and Reichlingia leopoldii. © 2018 W. Szafer Institute of Botany. All rights reserved. DA
