AB  - Investigations were carried out in spruce stands, 2 deciduous forests and an old orchard in SW Germany. Most species (47) are found in a Melico-Fagetum. Species spectra of spruce stands are very uniform. Abundance and biomass vary considerably during the season. Differences in ind/m2 between various ecosystems seem to be low, but high with respect to ind/g dry weight of substratum. Diversity of coenoses in spruce stands is far less than in other ecosystems. After liming plus fertilization, and after additional precipitation or after acidification, abundance decreases. Liming alone increases population density. -from English summary DA
