AU  - Podraza, P.
AU  - Schuhmacher, H.
T2  - Verhandlungen - Gesellschaft fur Okologie
AB  - Factors with major importance are: relocation and obstruction of the main stream, cutting off of the effluent discharges from a purification plant, storm water outlets, waste water and run off from farming and private buildings, ferroxide leeching from coal-mining dumps, alterations through ponds and impoundments and the discharge of warm and saline draining waters from coal-mining. Under these circumstances no stable benthic macrozoocoenosis has been developed. Most of the reaches show depauperated species composition as well as reduced individual numbers. The communities are almost entirely composed of ubiquitous forms with additional halotolerant and halophil species downstream from the saline flux. -from English summary DA
