TY  - JOUR
TI  - The influence of litter quantity and quality on the settlement abundance of Diptera larvae: an outdoor experiment in a limestone beechwood - the function of fauna in a mull beechwood 4
AU  - Hovemeyer, K.
T2  - Verhandlungen - Gesellschaft fur Okologie
AB  - In a beech forest near Gottingen, under high litter conditions, total dipteran larval abundance increased strongly (max. 15932 ind./m2) and a succession of abundance peaks was observed in particular families: Fanniidae and Lauxaniidae in 1982, Chironomidae in 1982 and 1983, Sciaridae in 1984. This succession is due to the change in nutritional quality of the increased leaf litter generations, which was quite pronounced compared to the stable conditions in the undisturbed litter layer. Structural features (litter accumulation) may hamper soil macrofauna activity, thus favouring dipterous larvae irrespective of other soil properties. -from English summary DA
