1535.
TY  - JOUR
TI  - Agriculture and eco-accounts - Pilot study for the integration of compensation measures into agricultural production
AU  - Höing, W.
AU  - Lenzen, W.
AU  - Steinhoff, J.
T2  - Naturschutz und Landschaftsplanung
AB  - For many years the city of Dortmund's industrial manufacturing infrastructure has been undergoing a transformation to that of a center for modern production and services providers. This process has been accompanied by high quality residential, cultural and recreational development. Although urban development planning strongly favors the re-use of the huge former areas of coal, iron and steel industries, the local farmers are seriously worried that urban expansion in the Eastern economic area 'Ruhr' would lead to a permanent loss of land, caused by unavoidable interventions into open space and the legally prescribed compensation of these interventions. To effectively counteract this trend the environmental authority of the city of Dortmund has commissioned a study how to actively integrate agriculture into compensation measures. The results of the pilot study show that the requirements of an ecologically and economically sustainable cultivation of compensation sites can be reconciled. For the region a catalogue of possible measurement packages has been compiled. First compensations measures have already been implemented in a pilot testing. Potential reservations of experts stating the renouncing of 'real compensation' in the approach described can be resolved with the amendment of the landscape conservation law of the Federal State of 'North Rhine-Westphalia' in June 2007. According to §4a the selection of compensation measures has to prefer those measures which aim to ecologically improve existing agricultural land-use and existing landscape structures. DA
