TI  - Succession of vegetation in abandoned fields in Finland.
AU  - Prach, K.
T2  - Annales Botanici Fennici
AB  - The species could be sorted roughly into 4 main groups, which were easily delimited in ordination space: annual weeds, perennial weed and ruderal species, meadow species, woody species and forest herbs. Species diversity declined with increasing latitude. The most variable aspects of the succession were initial species composition and time of invasion by woody species. Succession in abandoned fields in Finland usually proceeds rather rapidly toward forest communities, compared with that in drier parts of Central Europe. -from Author DA
