AB  - Canoeing enables many people to experience nature, but it also penetrates into ecologically sensitive areas that are valuable retreats for protected animal and plant species. This creates conflicts that can only be resolved by increasingly differentiated regulations. On German waterways, there are currently more than 1,000 individual regulations restricting access for canoeing. Very often, these regulations are not coordinated between neighbouring communities, which makes the practical implementation of the regulations difficult and meets With little understanding among kayakers and canoeists. Intercommunal cooperation and collaborative approaches, in which nature conservation and sports associa- tions work together constructively, are still rare. © 2020 Westermann Schulbuchverlag GmbH. All rights reserved. DA
