TI  - Changes in the Desmid communities of the Barssee and Pechsee natural reserves during the last seventy years with anthropic activity
AU  - Scheer, T
AU  - Kusber, WH
T2  - NOVA HEDWIGIA
AB  - The desmids of two bog areas in a reserve in urban Berlin, Germany were investigated in 1993. In Barssee and Pechsee 57 taxa were found among Sphagnum and in the plankton. At both sampling sites desmids were important contributors to the microalgal flora. The phytoplankton of Pechsee reached biovolumes up to 60 mm(3).l(-1) and was dominated by Cosmarium sphagnicolum throughout the entire vegetation period. In the plankton desmid species diversity was poor. But the Sphagnum-stands were rich in desmid species typical for oligotrophic and mesotrophic habitats. Taxa lists are compared to earlier investigations since 1923. Changes in the desmid nora are discussed in relation to fall of ground water level accompanying urbanization and restoration measures since 1985. This case study of the protection of species within an urban nature reserve shows the urgent need for a protection of Sphagnum-stands as habitats of diverse desmid communities. DA
