TI  - Realising the Kyffhäuser large-scale conservation project
AU  - Pusch, J.
T2  - Natur und Landschaft
AB  - The Kyffhäuser large-scale conservation project was implemented from 1997 to 2008. Funding allocated to this project totalled h 5.9 million. The Kyffhäuserkreis district authority was the agency responsible for the preparation of the management plan. While preparing the plan, it became apparent that the area is a biodiversity hotspot in Central Europe. Some 1,000 endangered species are found here. The district authority bought, in total, approx. 667 hectares of private land. The majority of this land is leased to farmers for extensive use. In line with nature protection and landscape conservation objectives, 727 hectares of oligotrophic grassland, orchards und woodland are managed in an extensive manner. Near the town of Bad Frankenhausen an orchard with 1,200 fruit trees representing 500 very old varieties has been planted. © 2010 W. Kohlhammer, Stuttgart. DA
