AU  - Versteirt, V
T2  - JOURNAL OF PEST SCIENCE
AB  - In Belgium, the current distribution and abundance of Xylosandrus germanus (Coleoptera, Scolytidae), a relatively new species to the Belgian fauna, is poorly known. Therefore, data on the range and population levels of this ambrosia beetle, on a regional and local scale respectively, are presented. Based on those results, the beetles' range is discussed. Among the analysed biotic and abiotic factors that could influence the species' settlement and population levels, climatic ones, and temperature in particular, seem to exert a crucial influence. DA
