AU  - Perner, J.
AU  - Marstaller, R.
T2  - Zeitschrift fur Okologie und Naturschutz
AB  - After the closure of a phosphate fertilizer factory the vegetation development of three differently polluted sampling sites were observed over a period of 10 years. During this time species richness increased dramatically in a heavily degraded and a degraded site. Only an insignificant increase was noticed in a moderately degraded site. The evenness increased in all examined sites. In the moderately degraded site no major changes in the proportion of CSR-types occurred during the 10 year period, while considerable changes were noticed in the degraded and heavily degraded site. At these sites there were differential changes in three categories; "stress tolerant ruderals" and "competitive ruderals" decreased and "competitors" increased from 1990 to 1999. The changing importance of allogenic and autogenic processes in succession is emphasized using the sampling sites as an example. DA
