AU  - Schlutter, M.
T2  - Aufbereitungs-Technik/Mineral Processing
AB  - The Raw Material Day was held at the Potsdam Chamber of Industry and Commerce, Brandenburg on 14th September 2016. The event offered a wide range of topics dealing with the utilization of domestic raw materials, power generation, raw material securing, biodiversity and the social acceptance of the raw material economy. The lectures particularly dealt with the utilization of lignite and its economic importance for Lusatia as well as with the trends of development towards a long term demand for raw material for the building industry. Thomas Weber from Cemex Zement GmbH explained that it is quite possible to combine raw material extraction and the protection of species demonstrated by the example of the limestone quarry at RuA&dersdorf. Dr.Jens Nissen from the Beeskow-based Bayerngas GmbH reported on the log process to the acceptance and the handling of the justified demands of a citizen’s initiative as planned drilling for natural gas extraction was approaching. Bert Vulpius, managing director of the UVMB, critically investigated the topic of the securing of raw material deposits within the framework of the state and regional planning in Brandenburg. DA
