AB  - Eastern England is planning to start big construction projects to inspire locals, attract visitors, and educate people about their local environment. First of the four projects is the East Reef, a promenade that will stretch 260m out into the sea at Jaywick in Essex. The project aims to encourage tourism, and raise awareness about coastal flooding. The second is a Dragonfly bridge that will flit around the region's waterway to be used as a focus for riverside events in various locations. The Lost Town project aims to create sculpture of a church on its original Anglo-Saxon site. The design of the Bridge of Reeds is inspired by the region's reelbeds and birds in flight. DA
